# Server Architecture - Complete Reference

## Server Overview

**Tech Stack**:
- Node.js with Express
- TypeORM with SQLite
- FFmpeg for video processing
- Firebase Admin for auth verification
- Windows-specific features (Recycle Bin via `trash`, file explorer)

**Port**: 4000 (configurable via PORT env var)

## Database

### TypeORM Entities

#### Clip Entity (`entity/Clip.ts`)
```typescript
{
  id: number;                    // Primary key
  filePath: string;              // Absolute path on disk (unique)
  relPath: string;               // Relative to VIDEOS_ROOT (indexed)
  game: string;                  // Top-level folder name (indexed)
  filename: string;              // File basename
  displayName: string | null;    // User-defined name
  extension: string;             // File extension (mp4, mov)
  sizeBytes: number;             // File size
  fileModifiedAt: Date;          // File modification time (indexed)
  createdAt: Date;               // Record creation time
  updatedAt: Date;               // Record update time
  published: boolean;            // Published status
  publishedUrl: string | null;   // Public URL when published
  starred: boolean;              // Starred status
  notes: string | null;          // Markdown notes
  tags: Tag[];                   // Many-to-many relation
}
```

#### Tag Entity (`entity/Tag.ts`)
```typescript
{
  id: number;                    // Primary key
  name: string;                  // Tag name (unique)
}
```

#### Collection Entity (`entity/Collection.ts`)
```typescript
{
  id: number;                    // Primary key
  name: string;                  // Collection name
  createdAt: Date;               // Creation time
  updatedAt: Date;               // Update time
  clips: Clip[];                 // Many-to-many relation
}
```

### Data Source Configuration
- **Database**: SQLite file at `DB_PATH` (default: `VIDEOS_ROOT/filmpje.db`)
- **Migrations**: Auto-sync enabled
- **Logging**: false in production
- **Connection**: Initialized on startup

## Core Services

### 1. Video Service (`services/videoService.ts`)

**Purpose**: Core video operations and file management

**Methods**:

#### Scanning & Syncing
- `scanAndSyncClips()`: 
  - Scans VIDEOS_ROOT for mp4/mov files
  - Creates/updates database records
  - Removes records for deleted files
  - Returns scan statistics

#### Video Processing
- `getClipMeta(clipId)`: Extract metadata with FFprobe
- `trimAndSwapClip(clipId, startSec, endSec)`: 
  - Create trimmed copy with FFmpeg
  - Replace original file
  - Update database
- `openClip(clipId)`: Open in default player (Windows `start`)

#### Cache Management
- `ensureThumbnail(clip)`: Generate thumbnail if not exists
- `ensureFrameStrip(clip)`: Generate frame strip if not exists
- `removeClipCaches(filePath)`: Delete thumbnail and frame strip

#### File Operations
- `moveClipFileToTrash(filePath)`: Move to Recycle Bin
- `moveClipToGame(clip, targetGame)`: Move file to different game folder

**Cache Locations**:
- Thumbnails: `VIDEOS_ROOT/.thumbnails/`
- Frame strips: `VIDEOS_ROOT/.frame-strips/`

### 2. Tag Patterns Service (`services/tagPatternsDb.ts`)

**Purpose**: Manage smart tag patterns in SQLite

**Database**: Separate SQLite file: `VIDEOS_ROOT/tag-patterns.db`

**Schema**:
```typescript
{
  tag: string;                   // Tag name (primary key)
  patterns: string;              // JSON array of regex patterns
  category: TagCategory;         // General|Gameplay|Weapons|Maps|Modes|Quality
}
```

**Methods**:
- `getAllPatterns()`: Load all patterns
- `addPattern(tag, patterns, category)`: Create new pattern
- `updatePattern(tag, patterns, category)`: Update existing pattern
- `removePattern(tag)`: Delete pattern

**Pattern Matching**:
- Patterns can be simple words (converted to word boundary regex)
- Or explicit regex patterns
- Used for automatic tag suggestions based on filename

### 3. Publisher Service (in publisher microservice)

**Purpose**: Handle clip publishing to public location

**Port**: 5000 (configurable)

**Storage**: `UPLOAD_DIR` (default: `publisher/public/`)

**Features**:
- Static file serving with cache headers
- Cloudflare cache purging support
- Upload management
- File deletion

## API Routes

### Clips Routes (`routes/clips.ts`)

**List Clips**:
- `GET /api/clips`
- Query params: `game`, `q` (search), `tags`, `published`, `starred`, `page`, `pageSize`
- Returns paginated results with total count

**Get Single Clip**:
- `GET /api/clips/:id`
- Returns clip with tags array

**Stream Video**:
- `GET /api/clips/:id/stream`
- Supports HTTP Range requests
- Proper video/* content type

**Get Thumbnail**:
- `GET /api/clips/:id/thumbnail`
- Generates if not exists
- Long cache duration

**Get Frame Strip**:
- `GET /api/clips/:id/frame-strip`
- For trim page preview
- Long cache duration

**Get Metadata**:
- `GET /api/clips/:id/meta`
- Returns FFprobe metadata

**Update Clip**:
- `PATCH /api/clips/:id`
- Body: `{ displayName?, tags?, notes? }`
- Returns updated clip

**Delete Clip**:
- `DELETE /api/clips/:id`
- Unpublishes if published
- Moves to Recycle Bin
- Cleans up empty folders

**Open Clip**:
- `POST /api/clips/:id/open`
- Opens in default player

**Trim Clip**:
- `POST /api/clips/:id/trim`
- Body: `{ startSec, endSec }`
- Re-encodes video

**Publish/Unpublish**:
- `POST /api/clips/:id/publish`
- `POST /api/clips/:id/unpublish`

**Star/Unstar**:
- `POST /api/clips/:id/star`
- `POST /api/clips/:id/unstar`

**Move to Game**:
- `POST /api/clips/:id/move-to-game`
- Body: `{ targetGame }`

**Export Audio**:
- `POST /api/clips/:id/export-audio`
- Returns audio file path

**Get Collections**:
- `GET /api/clips/:id/collections`
- Returns array of collection IDs

**Reveal in Explorer**:
- `POST /api/clips/reveal-file`
- Body: `{ filePath }`

**Import Files**:
- `POST /api/clips/import`
- Multipart form data
- Returns import results

**Export Timeline**:
- `POST /api/clips/export`
- Body: `{ clips: [], outputName?, exportId? }`
- Returns new clip object

**Export Progress**:
- `GET /api/clips/export/:exportId/progress`
- Returns progress percentage

**Batch Operations**:
- `POST /api/clips/batch/star`
- `POST /api/clips/batch/publish`
- `POST /api/clips/batch/add-tags`
- `POST /api/clips/batch/delete`

### Collections Routes (`routes/collections.ts`)

**List Collections**:
- `GET /api/collections`
- Returns all collections with clip counts

**Create Collection**:
- `POST /api/collections`
- Body: `{ name }`

**Update Collection**:
- `PATCH /api/collections/:id`
- Body: `{ name }`

**Delete Collection**:
- `DELETE /api/collections/:id`

**Get Collection Clips**:
- `GET /api/collections/:id/clips`
- Query params: same as clips list
- Returns paginated clips

**Add Clip to Collection**:
- `POST /api/collections/:collectionId/clips/:clipId`

**Remove Clip from Collection**:
- `DELETE /api/collections/:collectionId/clips/:clipId`

### Games Routes (`routes/games.ts`)

**List Games**:
- `GET /api/games`
- Returns array of `{ game, count }`
- Aggregated from clips table

### Stats Routes (`routes/stats.ts`)

**Get Statistics**:
- `GET /api/stats`
- Returns comprehensive statistics:
  - Total clips, size, averages
  - Published/starred counts
  - Tagged clips count
  - Per-game statistics
  - Most used tags
  - Last 14 days activity

### Tags Routes (`routes/tags.ts`)

**List All Tags**:
- `GET /api/tags`
- Returns unique tag names

**Delete Tag**:
- `DELETE /api/tags/:tagName`
- Removes tag from all clips

**Tag Patterns**:
- `GET /api/tag-patterns`
- `POST /api/tag-patterns`
- `PATCH /api/tag-patterns/:tag`
- `DELETE /api/tag-patterns/:tag`

## Actions Pattern

All business logic is encapsulated in Action classes:

**Base Action** (`actions/BaseAction.ts`):
```typescript
abstract class BaseAction<TInput, TOutput> {
  abstract execute(input: TInput): Promise<TOutput>;
}
```

**Example Actions**:
- `PublishClipAction`: Upload clip to publisher
- `UnpublishClipAction`: Remove clip from publisher
- `TrimAndSwapClipAction`: Trim video and replace
- `ExportTimelineAction`: Compile multiple clips
- `ScanAndSyncClipsAction`: Scan file system
- `ImportFilesAction`: Import uploaded files
- `BatchOperationsAction`: Various batch operations
- `ExportAudioAction`: Extract audio track
- `MoveClipToGameAction`: Move clip to different game
- `GetClipCollectionsAction`: Get clip's collections

## Middleware

### 1. Firebase Auth Middleware (`auth.ts`)
- Verifies Firebase JWT token
- Extracts user ID
- Protects all routes except `/api/health`
- Returns 401 if invalid/missing token

### 2. Error Handler Middleware (`middlewares/errorHandler.ts`)
- Catches all errors
- Logs to console
- Returns formatted error response
- Handles TypeORM errors specially

## Startup Sequence

1. Initialize TypeORM data source
2. Clean up empty folders in VIDEOS_ROOT
3. Run initial scan and sync
4. Sync with publisher service
5. Start Express server on configured port

## Video Processing

### FFmpeg Operations

**Thumbnail Generation**:
```bash
ffmpeg -i input.mp4 -vf "select=eq(n\,0)" -vframes 1 output.jpg
```

**Frame Strip Generation**:
```bash
ffmpeg -i input.mp4 -vf "select='not(mod(n\,N))',scale=120:-1" -frames:v 10 output%d.jpg
# Then combine frames into single strip
```

**Trimming**:
```bash
ffmpeg -ss START -to END -i input.mp4 -c:v libx264 -preset fast -crf 23 -c:a aac -b:a 192k output.mp4
```

**Timeline Export**:
- Creates temporary text file with clip list
- Uses FFmpeg concat demuxer
- Applies volume filters per clip
- Re-encodes to consistent format

**Audio Export**:
```bash
ffmpeg -i input.mp4 -vn -acodec mp3 -ab 192k output.mp3
```

## File System Operations

### Folder Structure
```
VIDEOS_ROOT/
├── GameName1/
│   ├── clip1.mp4
│   └── clip2.mov
├── GameName2/
│   └── clip3.mp4
├── .thumbnails/
│   ├── clip1.jpg
│   ├── clip2.jpg
│   └── clip3.jpg
├── .frame-strips/
│   ├── clip1.jpg
│   ├── clip2.jpg
│   └── clip3.jpg
├── filmpje.db
└── tag-patterns.db
```

### Cleanup
- Empty game folders are removed after clip deletion
- Caches are invalidated on clip modification
- Recycle Bin used for safety (not permanent deletion)

